// N108: per-query split-K QSA prompt attention for Intel Xe2 (Arc Pro B70) as a torch XPU op library
// (torch.ops.n108qsa.*), reading K/V in place from the paged pool through the physical token slots (no gather copy,
// no union, no host sync).
//
// Kernel 1 ("strata") is a port of Strata's per-query QSA attention (attn_chunk_kernel + attn_merge_kernel,
// launcher qsa_decode_attn_batch) from sycl/src/kernels/cuda/qsa_decode_attn.dp.cpp of
// github.com/Niko1221/Strata (HEAD 82f46a8), adapted to this server's KV format and semantics:
//   * KV pool [slots, Hk, 256] in fp8 e4m3fn (decoded in-kernel), bf16 or fp16, no scales (Strata: FP16 / INT8 /
//     Q4_0 through a page table); the cell -> pool row map is the physical token slot itself (slot < 0 = masked);
//   * q bf16 [rows, Hq, 256] (Strata: fp32), output bf16 [rows, Hq, 256];
//   * softmax over each row's valid slots only, rows without any valid slot -> exact 0 (SGLang
//     qsa_sparse_attention_reference semantics, as the union / Triton paths of n107-qsa);
//   * chunks per work-group (cpw) is a parameter: cpw = 1 is Strata's split-K (one 64-cell chunk per work-group,
//     log-sum-exp merge kernel); cpw = all chunks keeps one work-group per (row, kv head), online softmax across its
//     chunks and no merge (prefill has rows x Hk work-groups, enough parallelism without split-K).
// Kernel 2 ("bcast") keeps Strata's structure (q of one kv head's 12 query heads in SLM, chunk scores -> chunk
// softmax -> P.V with one thread per dimension, fp32 throughout) but computes Q.K with one LANE per cell: each
// sub-group takes SG cells, walks the 256 dimensions in blocks of SG, loads its q slice once per block and
// broadcasts it lane by lane (no cross-lane reductions, q read from SLM once per SG cells instead of once per cell).
// Chunk = 256 cells.
//
// Precision: fp32 scores, softmax (exp2 with log2(e) folded into the scale), P and accumulation; bf16 output (RNE).
// fp8 decode: mode 0 = exact integer decode to fp32; mode 1 = bits -> fp16 (exact: every e4m3fn value / 256 is an
// fp16 value; the 256 is folded into the q scale and the output normalisation). NaN codes (0x7f/0xff) are not
// produced by the KV writer; they decode to finite values (480 / 448-range), like the Triton kernels.
//
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
// Portions (kernel 1, the merge kernel) derived from Strata:
//
// MIT License
